{"schema_version":"1.0","language":"en","edition":"en-ak","revision":"0","book":{"position":19,"code":"PSA","name":"Psalms","testament":"OT"},"chapter":90,"content":[{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":["Book IV "]},{"type":"para","marker":"d","content":["A Prayer of Moses the man of God. "]},{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"1","sid":"PSA 90:1"},"LORD, thou hast been our dwelling place in all generations. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 90:1"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"2","sid":"PSA 90:2"},"Before the mountains were brought forth, or ever thou hadst formed the earth and the world, even from everlasting to everlasting, thou ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["art "]},"God. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 90:2"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"3","sid":"PSA 90:3"},"Thou turnest man to destruction; and sayest, Return, ye children of men. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 90:3"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"4","sid":"PSA 90:4"},"For a thousand years in thy sight ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are but"]}," as yesterday when it is past, and ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["as"]}," a watch in the night. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 90:4"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"5","sid":"PSA 90:5"},"Thou carriest them away as with a flood; they are ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["as"]}," a sleep: in the morning ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["they are"]}," like grass ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["which"]}," groweth up. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 90:5"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"6","sid":"PSA 90:6"},"In the morning it flourisheth, and groweth up; in the evening it is cut down, and withereth. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 90:6"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"7","sid":"PSA 90:7"},"For we are consumed by thine anger, and by thy wrath are we troubled. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 90:7"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"8","sid":"PSA 90:8"},"Thou hast set our iniquities before thee, our secret ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["sins "]},"in the light of thy countenance. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 90:8"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"9","sid":"PSA 90:9"},"For all our days are passed away in thy wrath: we spend our years as a tale ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["that is told."]},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 90:9"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"10","sid":"PSA 90:10"},"The days of our years ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," threescore years and ten; and if by reason of strength ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["they be"]}," fourscore years, yet ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," their strength labour and sorrow; for it is soon cut off, and we fly away. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 90:10"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"11","sid":"PSA 90:11"},"Who knoweth the power of thine anger? even according to thy fear, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["so is"]}," thy wrath. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 90:11"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"12","sid":"PSA 90:12"},"So teach ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["us"]}," to number our days, that we may apply ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["our "]},"hearts unto wisdom. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 90:12"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"13","sid":"PSA 90:13"},"Return, O LORD, how long? and let it repent thee concerning thy servants. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 90:13"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"14","sid":"PSA 90:14"},"O satisfy us early with thy mercy; that we may rejoice and be glad all our days. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 90:14"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"15","sid":"PSA 90:15"},"Make us glad according to the days ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["wherein"]}," thou hast afflicted us, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," the years ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["wherein"]}," we have seen evil. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 90:15"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"16","sid":"PSA 90:16"},"Let thy work appear unto thy servants, and thy glory unto their children. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 90:16"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"17","sid":"PSA 90:17"},"And let the beauty of the LORD our God be upon us: and establish thou the work of our hands upon us; yea, the work of our hands establish thou it. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 90:17"}]}]}
